Ladybird’s prompt offers Chrome’s three answers, with the same labels
(IDS_PERMISSION_ALLOW_WHILE_VISITING, IDS_PERMISSION_ALLOW_THIS_TIME,
and IDS_PERMISSION_NEVER_ALLOW in permissions_strings.grdp), anchored to
the location bar as Chrome’s permission bubble is. Gecko’s geolocation
prompt (GeolocationPermissionPrompt in PermissionUI.sys.mjs) has Allow
and Block with a “Remember this decision” box instead, and also adds
a hint line when the system will ask next, as Ladybird’s does. WebKit’s
iOS prompt has Allow and Don’t Allow.
